Given the function $f(x)=\ln (x+a)-x$, where $a\in R$.
(1) Find the monotonic intervals of $f(x)$ when $a=-1$;
(2) Find the range of values of the real number $a$ such that the inequality $e^{f(x)}+ \frac {a}{2}x^{2} > 1$ holds when $x\geqslant 1$.

