\right.\]
Find the maximum value of the function $g$.

Given the function $f(x) = e^{x} - 3x^{2} + ax$, the equation of the tangent line to its graph at $x=1$ is $y = (e-2)x + b$.  
$(1)$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$;  
$(2)$ If the inequality $f(x) > m$ holds for all $x \in [1, +\infty)$, find the maximum integer value of $m$. (Reference data: $\ln 10 \approx 2.3$)

